From: Niravkumar L Rabara <niravkumarlaxmidas.rabara@altera.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] cpu_init: guard ICC_SRE_EL2 under HV_GUEST_EL1

ICC_SRE_EL2 is an EL2/EL3-only system register. A hypervisor that lands
its guest at EL1 (e.g. Bao) has already programmed ICC_SRE_EL2.SRE on the
guest's behalf, so the MSR ICC_SRE_EL2 in _core_setup is UNDEFINED when
executed from EL1 (not a trap to EL2 - the exception is taken right back
into the guest's own sync-exception vector). On Bao that vector just
spins, so the guest hangs before producing any output.

Guard the write with #ifndef HV_GUEST_EL1. The currentEL dispatch that
follows already handles an EL1 entry, and ICC_SRE_EL1 is still programmed
so the guest's own GIC system-register access is set up as before.
With HV_GUEST_EL1=OFF (the default) the emitted code is unchanged.

Ported from patches/v26.1-SMP/0001; v26.3 reworked the comment style and
register ordering around this MSR, so the original context no longer
matched.

Signed-off-by: Niravkumar L Rabara <niravkumarlaxmidas.rabara@altera.com>
---
diff --git a/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S b/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S
index d5f42c4..a4773f5 100644
--- a/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S
+++ b/FreeRTOS/Demo/SOCFPGA/startup/cpu_init.S
@@ -167,7 +167,16 @@ _core_setup:
     MOV x1, #1
 
     ISB
+#ifndef HV_GUEST_EL1
+    /* ICC_SRE_EL2 is only accessible from EL2/EL3. When this image is built
+     * as a hypervisor guest that enters at EL1 (HV_GUEST_EL1=ON, e.g. for
+     * Bao), ICC_SRE_EL2.SRE has already been programmed by the hypervisor;
+     * executing this MSR from EL1 is UNDEFINED (not a trap to EL2 - the
+     * exception is taken right back into this guest's own sync-exception
+     * vector), and on Bao that vector just spins. Skip the write entirely -
+     * the currentEL fallthrough below handles the EL1 entry path. */
     MSR ICC_SRE_EL2, x0
+#endif
     ISB
     /* SRE = 1, Enable the Ssystem register interface for the current security level. */
     MSR ICC_SRE_EL1, x1
